cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  PAER-LLM: A Unified Psychoacoustic-Semantic Representation for
  Speech Emotion Recognition
message: >-
  If you use this software or the evaluation harness, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gaurav
    family-names: Sharma
    email: gaurav.vit08@gmail.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/<user>/paer-llm'
abstract: >-
  Code and evaluation harness for a controlled study of evaluation
  protocol effects in speech emotion recognition on RAVDESS. Holding
  architecture and hyperparameters fixed and varying only the data
  partitioning, reported accuracy moves 30.5 points, while the largest
  difference between three fusion operators is 2.03 points - below the
  design's 3.47-point minimum detectable effect. Includes actor-disjoint
  splitting utilities with published fold assignments, a corpus-integrity
  check, the contaminated-protocol reproduction, and stream
  complementarity and calibration analyses.
keywords:
  - speech emotion recognition
  - evaluation protocol
  - data leakage
  - speaker-independent evaluation
  - psychoacoustic features
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
